Welcome to our first report! Err... well, it's mostly just me (Lead) during this period. This report is for the first 2 months, to get you all up to speed with everything that has already been done so far. Later reports will be made for each month.

As with any game translation project starting out, most of the time was spent on hacking the game and developing the tools needed to translate the game. The first order of business was to get the game to properly render English text. The first attempt looked something like this:

![AAAAAAAAAAAAAAA]({image1})

<center>
    <small>Sorry I just wanted to include this image</small>
</center>

The game was able to render ASCII characters without any direct code modification, so at least I had some work cut out for me. Obviously though, this was designed for a completely different writing system, therefore I had to replace the entire text rendering procedure so that it renders English text nicely and in the right direction. On top of that, there was a pretty nasty limitation on how much text it can hold on a single page due to how the memory was used, so in the end, I basically gutted out the game's entire text processing system and made some very heavy modifications. The font was also replaced because the original one was designed to be monospaced, which did not make for a very good reading experience. The end result looks pretty good though, so it was all worth it. (Note: very early development screenshot)

![Beautiful text rendering]({image2})

I also had to create a script assembler that was used to modify the script you're seeing here, among other miscellaneous tools. The script assembler produces translation documents that can be used to modify the strings in the scripts, with auto text wrapping, which will be reassembled back into the script. The translation documents are nothing more than regular text files, with a custom format that was designed for this specific use case, making it a breeze to work on the game's translations.

![Translation document]({image3})

With all of that done, all that's left to do was to actually translate the game. Admittedly, I probably shouldn't have done any of this myself, but I initially thought that everything this game had to offer was all taken from the novel, which has already been translated well beyond the contents of this game. So I just took it upon myself to assemble the novel translations into the game's scripts.

Little did I know though, I would soon encounter unique stories that have never been included in any other media before. Additionally, due to the presentation format of this game, quite a bit of modifications had to be done to the translations, which is something that I was not qualified to do and absolutely despised doing.

Regardless, I was able to finish translating 4 chapters: chapter 1, 3 and 4, plus the prologue. These were all stories taken directly from the novel. There is a total of 12 chapters in the game, along with some other textual content, so that makes it about 30% done in terms of text translations. Most of the game's UI has also been translated.

The project would've ended here, rotting away in my backlog, if not for the translators who offered their help during my last ditch attempt to continue the project. I probably should have looked for help since the beginning, but back then, I thought that there were no interested translators left in the community, seeing that the novel translations have been at a standstill for quite a while.

But of course, you never really know unless you try, so I'm glad that my Reddit gambit turned out well and there were actual translators finding out about my project. I also happened to stumble upon the [Anime Game Translations Team](https://agtteam.net/), whose name made it seem like they could be interested in my project, so I decided to have a go in their Discord server. I was really glad that they were welcoming people like me who were looking for help with their own projects, and supported me throughout the discussion.

So once again, special thanks to everyone on the r/KinoNoTabi subreddit who helped the post achieve the level of reach it needed, and the AGT Team for letting me have that discussion, you all may have single-handedly saved the project.

That's all for now. Tune in next month where we'll be updating you on our translation progress!